diff --git a/docs/storage-usage.md b/docs/storage-usage.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1925b54
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/storage-usage.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Storage usage
+
+`Account#bytes_used` and `Board#bytes_used` return integer byte counts from
+background-maintained totals (zero before anything has been counted). Each call
+reads the current total, including on an already-loaded account or board.
+
+Counted attachments are card images and Active Storage embeds in board public
+descriptions, card descriptions, and comment bodies. Each attachment occurrence
+counts its blob's original byte size, including when a blob is reused. Avatars,
+exports/imports, unattached uploads, remote images, previews, and generated
+variants do not count. Draft cards count too.
+
+## Updating totals
+
+Attachment creation/removal persists an accounting entry or marks one pending in
+the same database transaction. Jobs reconcile individual entries against current
+attachment existence and board membership. Card moves mark the card's entries
+(including comments) pending in the move transaction.
+
+A worker locks the entry and atomically applies only the difference to account
+and board totals before clearing the pending flag. Retries, duplicate jobs,
+reordered jobs, and rolled-back changes cannot double count. Removals retain the
+previously accounted size until reconciliation, even if the blob has been purged.
+Detached entries are deleted once reconciled. Zero-valued totals for deleted
+boards remain until account deletion so outstanding deltas can safely settle.
+
+Reads use one indexed lookup, not an attachment scan. Normal attachment changes
+reconcile one entry, with no account-wide counter lock in the request. Workers
+use atomic increments for totals; unrelated entries can be processed concurrently.
+Backfill and card-move work is split into batches of at most 1,000 entries. The
+recurring recovery sweep processes up to 1,000 pending entries each minute if an
+original job was missed.
+
+Totals are eventually consistent: they reflect committed changes after workers
+process the corresponding jobs, not necessarily within the request that made a
+change. Workers and the recurring scheduler must be running.
+
+## Existing installations and imports
+
+After deploying and migrating an existing installation, run:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails storage:backfill
+```
+
+This enqueues resumable, bounded background batches for each account. It is safe
+to rerun while users are active; already tracked attachments are not counted
+again. Account imports automatically enqueue the same backfill after importing
+records because bulk inserts bypass model callbacks. Accounting tables are
+derived data and are not included in account exports.
